  era: "Section 18 \xB7 Arrival of Europeans \xB7 1498 \u2013 1760s"
  title: European rivalry
  text: European companies fought one another and joined Indian politics. The Anglo-French Carnatic Wars, from 1746 to 1763, showed that small European-trained armies could decide Indian successions, a lesson the British used to expand their power.
